  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Toofan wanted to write the string `\"ADVITIYA\"`, but accidentally wrote the 8-letter string SSS instead.   He wants to correct his mistake with the minimum number of steps.\n\nIn one step, Toofan can choose an index iii (1≤i≤N1 \\leq i \\leq N1≤i≤N), and change SiS_iSi​ to the next letter in the alphabet.\n\nThat is, change A→B,B→C,C→D\\text{A} \\to \\text{B}, \\text{B} \\to \\text{C}, \\text{C} \\to \\text{D}A→B,B→C,C→D, and so on.\n\nThe alphabet is considered cyclic, so Z\\text{Z}Z can be changed to A\\text{A}A.\n\nFor example, if SSS equals `\"ZARAGOZA\"`,\n\n\nOperating on the first index will turn SSS into `\"AARAGOZA\"`.\nOperating on the second index will instead turn SSS into `\"ZBRAGOZA\"`.\nOperating on the third index will instead turn SSS into `\"ZASAGOZA\"`.\n\nAnd so on for the other indices.\nFind the minimum number of steps required to convert the string SSS into `\"ADVITIYA\"`.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line contains an integer TTT — the number of test cases.\nThe next TTT lines each contain a string SSS consisting of exactly 888 uppercase English letters.\n\n\nOutput Format\n\nFor each test case, output a single integer on a new line — the minimum number of steps to convert SSS into `\"ADVITIYA\"`.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤10001 \\leq T \\leq 10001≤T≤1000",
      "SSS has length 888.",
      "Each character of SSS is an uppercase English letter."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\nADVITIYA\nADVITIAA",
        "output": "0\n24",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: SSS already equals \"ADVITIYA\", so 000 steps are needed.\nTest case 222: \"ADVITIAA\" can be turned into \"ADVITIYA\" in 242424 steps, by repeatedly operating on the 777-th character.\nThat is, \"ADVITIAA\" becomes \"ADVITIBA\", then \"ADVITICA\", then \"ADVITIDA\", and so on till it reaches \"ADVITIYA\"."
      }
    ]
  },
